{
  "sticker": "ring",
  "called": "the rubber ring",
  "skeleton": "an inflatable ring tilted towards us: root under its lowest point; tip at its right edge (it tips up on one side); body at its centre; spin and turn at the centre too, so a turn of spin between body squashed to the ring's tilt and turn stretched back (sy 0.86 and 1/0.86) turns the ring round flat on the water, its outline unchanged and only its stripes going round.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of an inflatable swim ring. Draw it as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate pieces laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every piece at the size it has in image 1 (if they do not all fit, draw them all a little smaller, at the same scale as each other).\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no piece touching or overlapping another:\n1. the swim ring exactly as in image 1: red and white stripes, its round hole and its shine.\n2. the same swim ring turned round in its own plane by one stripe, so that every red stripe is where a white one was in image 1; the same outline, the same tilt and the shine in the same place.\n\nEvery piece is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another piece, with its edges clean and smooth. It is an object, not a character: no face, no eyes, no mouth. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the pieces beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows, no water, no sand, no splashes or drops. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
